{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Rotate the compromised GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN — BLOCKED on deploying the 66af fix to prod first\n\n## Why this exists\n66af (Gerrit 1384, MERGED) fixes the review-bot logging the webhook token in plaintext. Its\nAC5 mandates the already-leaked token be rotated AND that the rotation be \"TRACKED SEPARATELY\nAND EXPLICITLY\". This ticket is that record.\n\n## Decisive finding (do NOT rotate before deploying)\nThe 66af code is merged to main but NOT deployed to the prod box (i-00880b2c7f13527c5). Verified\ninside the running container `compose-review-bot-1` (image built 2026-08-04T11:07Z, BEFORE 1384\nmerged ~12:47):\n  - review_bot/config.py: TokenRedactingFilter  -> 0 (absent)\n  - review_bot/app.py:    X-Rebar-Token          -> 0 (absent)\n  - review_bot/app.py:243  token = request.query_params.get(\"token\", \"\")  <-- still URL-sourced\nSo the bot still takes the token from `?token=` and uvicorn access-logs it in clear text.\nRotating now would re-leak the NEW token the moment Gerrit's webhook/`/rerun` next calls it —\nexactly the runbook's forbidden precondition (\"the code fix must land BEFORE rotation\").\n\n## Also: the token is a SHARED secret (ADR-0014)\n`/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token` is simultaneously (a) the bot's Gerrit HTTP basic-auth password\n(outbound REST/voting), (b) the inbound webhook `?token=`/`X-Rebar-Token` secret, and (c) the\ncontainer `GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN` env. A bare `aws ssm put-parameter` DESYNCS these and breaks the\nLLM-Review gate. The canonical atomic tool is `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` (gerrit set-account\nnew password + SSM overwrite + re-render/push webhooks.config to refs/meta/config).\n\n## Correct sequence (coordinated deploy-then-rotate; brief review-bot bounce)\n1. Deploy current origin/main (with 66af) to the box: rebuild the `compose-review-bot` image\n   from current main + `docker compose up -d` recreate; re-render webhooks.config to the\n   X-Rebar-Token HEADER form via the updated service-user.sh. This removes the leaky URL path.\n2. Rotate: run `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` -> new 256-bit token set as the bot's Gerrit HTTP\n   password, overwritten into SSM, and substituted into webhooks.config (pushed to\n   refs/meta/config).\n3. Restart the review-bot container so it loads the new GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN (fetch-secrets.sh ->\n   .env -> compose up -d).\n4. Verify end-to-end: inbound webhook triggers a review (or `/rerun`), AND an outbound\n   LLM-Review vote succeeds (outbound basic-auth works). Update any operator-local git\n   credential caches to the new token.\n5. Prefer a quiet window AFTER in-flight changes 1376 (9305) and 1386 (1dbe) have landed — both\n   depend on the LLM-Review bot and would be disrupted by the bounce.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] 66af code deployed to the prod box; running container confirmed to source the token from\n      the X-Rebar-Token header and to carry TokenRedactingFilter (no `?token=` URL read).\n- [x] Token rotated via service-user.sh: new value is the bot's Gerrit HTTP password, in SSM,\n      and in the pushed webhooks.config; old (compromised) value no longer accepted.\n- [x] review-bot restarted and verified: an inbound webhook/`/rerun` triggers a review AND an\n      outbound LLM-Review vote lands with the new credential.\n- [x] Rotation recorded as DONE here (not assumed), and 66af AC5 checked off / closed.\n\n## Security note\nUntil step 2 completes, the previously-logged token remains COMPROMISED and valid. Treat as an\nopen credential exposure."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785892041479317001,"uuid":"602d2e1d-1598-4ede-9659-362c36a16b79"}